# Normalize text in the repository; check out with the platform's convention.
* text=auto

# Vendored code is checked out byte-for-byte, with no end-of-line translation.
# Two reasons: it is not ours to reformat, and scripts/vendor-manifest.sh is the
# only integrity check these modules have (they carry no go.sum entries — see
# THIRD_PARTY.md), so their bytes must not depend on the developer's git config.
vendor/** -text

# Shell scripts must be LF or they will not run on Linux, where CI runs them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# gofmt refuses to touch a file whose line endings aren't LF, so a Windows
# checkout (where `text=auto` alone checks out CRLF) makes gofmt -l flag every
# .go file as unformatted even when nothing was actually changed. Forcing LF
# here — the same fix already applied to *.sh — keeps `go/gofmt` usable on any
# platform and matches what's already stored in the repo (blobs are LF).
*.go text eol=lf

# Checksums and coverage floors are compared line by line across platforms.
*.sha256 text eol=lf
scripts/coverage-floors.txt text eol=lf
